  "name": "Example: Finding the Remainder in a Division Problem",
  "problem": "Use the model above to determine the missing fraction in the following division problem.\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/4814fdac6a7385adf0ba95cd488a7fe323a9d4c760e3462c2bd1bc3542a579ca.svg)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/e60ebf4ac02326cff610f1d4238bb2b8c16062aaa8a50c7cc040631e65d3a5b0.png)",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by interpreting our model:\n\n- The model shows $2$ wholes split into sixths.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/6c4328991ef5f89f91b3df5b4d43f8034d58249442700d59c2d842a44c9e8cda.png)\n\n- There are $\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{5}$ sixths in each group, with $\\bbox[2pt, Moccasin]{2}$ remaining.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/e08a28fee137c40615d7261b6282dce8dd0392084a8d801f9cc848364a3ad0f5.png)\n\nNote the following: \n\n- There are $\\color{red}2$ full groups.\n\n- There are $\\bbox[2pt, Moccasin]{2}$ sixths left over out of a possible group of $\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{5}.$ So the fractional part of our answer is \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\bbox[2pt, Moccasin]{2}}{\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{5}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n2 \\div \\dfrac{5}{6} = {\\color{red}{2}} \\, \\dfrac{\\bbox[2pt, Moccasin]{2}}{\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{5}}.\n$$",
